`isResourceQuotaConflict` identifies the transient quota conflict by checking for two English substrings in `err.Error()`. These strings are not an API contract. A change in apiserver wording, or an admission-plugin wrapper that alters the message, would silently turn the retry into a no-op. The user would then see the original flaky quota-conflict failure again, with no signal that the workaround stopped working. The match is also broader than it looks: any conflict whose message mentions `resourcequotas` is retried. The check could instead use `apierrors.StatusError.Status().Details.Kind == "resourcequotas"` (via `errors.As`), falling back to the substring only if Details are absent.

Suggestion: var se apierrors.APIStatus
