That changes the documented 'idle' semantics from closing only idle keep-alive sockets to forcibly closing every connection. Active in-flight requests are aborted mid-response during graceful shutdown. This affects the common case: default server plus `forceCloseConnections: 'idle'`.

Suggestion: if (forceCloseConnections === 'idle') {
