`eval` runs any user-supplied JavaScript, which allows remote code execution. ADR-0001 forbids this and requires formulas to go through a parser for the supported grammar. Use a small arithmetic parser for numbers, `+ - * /` and parentheses instead.

Improved code:
export function evaluate(formula: string): number {
  let pos = 0;
  const skip = (): void => {
    while (pos < formula.length && /\s/.test(formula[pos])) pos++;
  };
  function parseExpr(): number {
    let v = parseTerm();
    for (;;) {
      skip();
      const c = formula[pos];
      if (c === "+") { pos++; v += parseTerm(); }
      else if (c === "-") { pos++; v -= parseTerm(); }
      else return v;
    }
  }
  function parseTerm(): number {
    let v = parseFactor();
    for (;;) {
      skip();
      const c = formula[pos];
      if (c === "*") { pos++; v *= parseFactor(); }
      else if (c === "/") { pos++; v /= parseFactor(); }
      else return v;
    }
  }
  function parseFactor(): number {
    skip();
    const c = formula[pos];
    if (c === "(") {
      pos++;
      const v = parseExpr();
      skip();
      if (formula[pos] !== ")") throw new Error(`Expected ')' at ${pos}`);
      pos++;
      return v;
    }
    if (c === "-") { pos++; return -parseFactor(); }
    const m = /^\d+(\.\d+)?/.exec(formula.slice(pos));
    if (!m) throw new Error(`Unexpected token at ${pos}`);
    pos += m[0].length;
    return Number(m[0]);
  }
  const result = parseExpr();
  skip();
  if (pos !== formula.length) throw new Error(`Unexpected token at ${pos}`);
  return result;
}

If `WEBHOOK_SECRET` is missing, the code falls back to an empty HMAC key, so anyone can forge valid signatures. The `===` comparison also leaks timing information. Per ADR-0002, fail at startup when the secret is missing and compare with `crypto.timingSafeEqual`.

Improved code:
import { createHmac, timingSafeEqual } from "node:crypto";

const SECRET = process.env.WEBHOOK_SECRET;
if (!SECRET) {
  throw new Error("WEBHOOK_SECRET is not configured");
}

export function verifySignature(body: string, signature: string): boolean {
  const expected = Buffer.from(
    createHmac("sha256", SECRET as string).update(body).digest("hex"),
    "utf8",
  );
  const provided = Buffer.from(signature, "utf8");
  if (expected.length !== provided.length) {
    return false;
  }
  return timingSafeEqual(expected, provided);
}

