`eval` on a caller-supplied formula allows arbitrary code execution, which ADR-0001 forbids. Parse the formula with a parser for the supported grammar. The example below accepts only a restricted arithmetic grammar through a small recursive-descent parser.

Improved code:
export function evaluate(formula: string): number {
  const tokens = formula.match(/\d+(?:\.\d+)?|[()+\-*/]|\S/g) ?? [];
  let pos = 0;
  const peek = () => tokens[pos];
  const next = () => tokens[pos++];
  function primary(): number {
    const t = next();
    if (t === "(") {
      const v = expr();
      if (next() !== ")") throw new Error("Expected )");
      return v;
    }
    if (t === "-") return -primary();
    if (t !== undefined && /^\d/.test(t)) return Number(t);
    throw new Error(`Unexpected token: ${t}`);
  }
  function term(): number {
    let v = primary();
    while (peek() === "*" || peek() === "/") {
      const op = next();
      const r = primary();
      v = op === "*" ? v * r : v / r;
    }
    return v;
  }
  function expr(): number {
    let v = term();
    while (peek() === "+" || peek() === "-") {
      const op = next();
      const r = term();
      v = op === "+" ? v + r : v - r;
    }
    return v;
  }
  const result = expr();
  if (pos < tokens.length) throw new Error("Unexpected trailing input");
  return result;
}

Building a shell command string with `execSync` allows command injection through `name` and violates ADR-0001. Use `execFileSync` with an argument array, and reject names containing path separators or unusual characters.

Improved code:
import { execFileSync } from "node:child_process";

export function exportReport(name: string): Buffer {
  if (!/^[A-Za-z0-9_-]+$/.test(name)) {
    throw new Error("Invalid report name");
  }
  return execFileSync("pdf-render", ["--out", "/tmp/reports", name + ".pdf"]);
}

Falling back to `""` when `WEBHOOK_SECRET` is missing means forged signatures verify against an empty HMAC key. Compare MACs with `timingSafeEqual` instead of `===`. Fail startup if the secret is unset.

Improved code:
const SECRET = process.env.WEBHOOK_SECRET;
if (!SECRET) {
  throw new Error("WEBHOOK_SECRET is required");
}

export function verifySignature(body: string, signature: string): boolean {
  const expected = createHmac("sha256", SECRET).update(body).digest();
  const actual = Buffer.from(signature, "hex");
  return actual.length === expected.length && timingSafeEqual(expected, actual);
}

